  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nWidespread freeze is expected tonight into Tuesday morning as \nhigh pressure builds, resulting in diminishing wind and \nradiational cooling. With high confidence in low temperatures \nbelow freezing tonight into Tuesday morning, a Freeze Warning \nremains in effect areawide. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...\n\nA weak cold front is expected to move south across the region\nTuesday night into Wednesday, with scattered showers. Isolated\nthunderstorms are possible, though instability is progged to be\nlimited. A number of ensemble models indicate the highest \nchance for thunderstorms (but still only 15-30%) is south and \neast of Pittsburgh; lightning will likely be the only threat.\n\nRidging returns dry and warmer weather Thursday into early \nFriday. The ridge is expected to flatten by late week into the \nweekend, with a more zonal flow across much of the CONUS, and a \nclosed low across south central Canada. \n\nWeak shortwaves embedded in the flow are expected to cross the \nUpper Ohio Valley region late Friday and into the weekend. \nOccasional shower and thunderstorm chances are expected. \nHowever, the chances of severe thunderstorms is consider very \nlow due to the probability of strong vertical wind shear and \ninstability remaining below 10%.",
